  "task": {
    "id": "ohmyform-anonymous-ip-fallback",
    "prompt": "The submission-start flow must behave exactly as the following input/output\ntable describes. Regular submissions keep the form, user, and device, hash\nthe token through the injected hash dependency, and never store the raw IP\naddress. When the IP address is missing, the flow stores the existing\nmissing-IP placeholder ('?'). Anonymous submissions remove the user before\npersistence. No implementation approach is prescribed; only the observable\ninput/output behavior below is graded.\n\nInput/output table (command fields: form, user, token, device, ipAddr):\n- regular submission, ipAddr present -> user retained; stored IP differs\n  from the raw value.\n- regular submission, ipAddr absent -> user retained; stored IP is '?'.\n- anonymous submission, ipAddr present -> user removed; stored IP differs\n  from the raw value.\n- anonymous submission, ipAddr absent -> user removed; stored IP is '?'.\n\nProduce production-quality code: type-safe, no suppressed diagnostics, no\ndynamic code execution or process-spawning APIs."
  },
